e/aW1hZ2UvNDA2ODk3Ni8yNTU4NTg5NS5wbmc=/original/HZA7lO.png","text","mediaReviewed","Screenshot source reviewed","value","2026-10-20","image","gameplay","The author’s Godot play-mode screenshot, retaining the original editor and debug panels.","src","/GameMap/media/learning/deep-yellow-claude.webp","alt","A first-person yellow-corridor encounter with a held bat, inventory and minimap, inside the creator’s captured Godot editor.","https://aebrer.itch.io/deep-yellow","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","Creator-published screenshot","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)",[88],"Claude Code","Related resources",[93,94],"resourceIds","section",{"_59":96,"_25":97},{"_59":88,"_25":95},"/resources/claude-code/","Godot Engine · Official Documentation","/resources/godot-engine/","Creator evidence",[101],"evidence",{"_59":102,"_25":103,"_104":105},"Read the explicit Claude Code credit","https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/blob/master/CREDITS.md#code-and-design","note","Creator attribution specifically names Claude via Claude Code. The itch page separately discloses AI assistance for code; no complete session transcript is supplied.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[110],{"_59":111,"_25":112,"_104":113},"Open the complete Godot game","https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow","Full Godot 4.6 project, scenes, scripts, assets, shaders, and export presets. The itch page lists code MIT and assets CC0, while CREDITS.md still leaves the original-code license undecided and some third-party licenses unspecified; inspect both before reuse.","More ways to play",[117],"distribution",{"_59":118,"_25":119,"_104":120},"GitHub Releases","https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/releases/tag/v0.13.0","Download — Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.","Access type","playable","demo","Play or run",[126],{"_59":127,"_25":77,"_104":128},"Play DEEP YELLOW","In-development browser build plus Windows/Linux downloads. The creator recommends Chrome or a controller; Firefox mouse input has known problems. Includes horror themes and an interactive tutorial.","Game platform","itch.io","Guide format","build log","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[136],{"_59":137,"_25":77,"_104":-7},"Read the creator’s game and development notes","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[142,143,144,145],"Play the interactive tutorial and compare moving, waiting, equipment, and sanity.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the project’s separate attribution file.","Import project.godot in Godot 4.6 and inspect the start menu, procedural levels, and turn systems.","Change one equipment or turn rule, then test a complete run and restart.","AI workflow / foundation context","Drew Brereton identifies the game as code-assisted by Claude. The project credits specifically name Claude Code and distinguish original work from external shaders, textures, and fonts.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","3D","track","metadata","Engine","Godot 4.6 · GDScript","engine","lead","3d","ai-assisted",[142,143,144,145],{"_59":137,"_25":77,"_17":179},{"_59":127,"_25":77,"_17":122,"_104":128},{"_59":111,"_25":112,"_177":178,"_104":113},{"_59":102,"_25":103,"_104":105},[175,176],[171],{"_172":118,"_25":119,"_17":173,"_104":174},"platform","download","Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.","godot-engine","claude-code","scope","complete-project","build-log",{"_181":182},"documents",{"_183":184,"_185":186},"en",[188,192,193,194,191,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,202,203,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220,221,222,223,224,2